        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                "word": "genièvre",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "38610485-4e4b-4376-bc5d-188cc07e98db",
                        "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "genièvres"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cea82f98-da01-3c32-9341-70e1e2f6f5ca",
                        "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom vulgaire du genévrier commun, (Juniperus communis) arbuste odoriférant dont les feuilles sont cylindriques, un peu longues et pointues par le bout, et qui porte, comme le laurier, un petit fruit rond et noir."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0cd08ba-6192-4647-852a-80213c2a812c",
                                "sense_id": "cea82f98-da01-3c32-9341-70e1e2f6f5ca",
                                "text": "Bois de genièvre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "572ccb92-86ea-4dda-a646-a228b2e7a545",
                                "sense_id": "cea82f98-da01-3c32-9341-70e1e2f6f5ca",
                                "text": "Le monarque gisait encore tout près du trône, dans une épaisse fumée de genièvre que l’on dit agréable aux narines des morts."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1e08588-2d4c-3d38-989d-f1d2747c31ae",
                        "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cône bacciforme du genévrier commun : baie de genièvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a76896-5363-4011-a294-5cdb8695dc7b",
                                "sense_id": "e1e08588-2d4c-3d38-989d-f1d2747c31ae",
                                "text": "M. Helvétius indique une méthode différente ; il double la dose du genièvre concassé , supprime l'orge , et y substitue quatre poignées d’absinthe bien épluchée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a61a2b5-2f3f-455c-a5fa-ffee5b5fb7ce",
                                "sense_id": "e1e08588-2d4c-3d38-989d-f1d2747c31ae",
                                "text": "J’ai accompagné d’une demi-bouteille de champigny de la mousse de pintadeau au genièvre, une crépine de pied de porc aux lentilles, un sorbet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3051ecb3-8c24-38ec-a789-2ac20bbc517f",
                        "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Liqueur faite avec du grain de genièvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86d9c99b-98e0-4984-96c1-a62201afffca",
                                "sense_id": "3051ecb3-8c24-38ec-a789-2ac20bbc517f",
                                "text": "Je la pris dans mes bras, elle releva la tête en la balançant, puis elle me regarda, mais assurément sans me voir ; alors je respirai une odeur de genièvre qu’exhalait son haleine chaude. Je reculai. Elle laissa retomber sa tête sur ses deux bras étalés sur la table.\n— Gin, dit mon grand-père.\nEt il me regarda en ricanant, disant quelques mots que je ne compris pas."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0afd4abd-2810-487a-b17d-0b9faf90da05",
                                "sense_id": "3051ecb3-8c24-38ec-a789-2ac20bbc517f",
                                "text": "Le mariage des baies de genièvre avec un alcool fort (généralement de l’eau-de-vie, autrefois de l’absinthe) est consommé de longue date et a donné naissance en France au fameux genièvre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3172867-d2f9-4fdf-a217-f3e9548af169",
                                "sense_id": "3051ecb3-8c24-38ec-a789-2ac20bbc517f",
                                "text": "Alors il chercha l'oubli tour à tour dans le cidre normand, le poiré manceau, l’hydromel gaulois, le cognac français, le genièvre hollandais, le gin anglais, le wiskey écossais, le kirsch germain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c49522e-c310-4f0d-a600-44a1c7b3f7a7",
                                "sense_id": "3051ecb3-8c24-38ec-a789-2ac20bbc517f",
                                "text": "Pour faire cesser ce chagrin, son père adoptif lui donnait un biscuit trempé dans du péquet, le genièvre local."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75b9410e-d540-3691-a6d3-8afd088b7951",
                        "entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bois du genévrier commun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2faeca67-c077-4890-92a4-ec94d4b46114",
                        "source_entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "source_sense_description": "genévrier : voir genévrier",
                        "target_lang_word": "Machandelbaum",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "25ad779c-642c-49ad-b75e-6cfc0352d1ac",
                        "source_entry_id": "6cf76d80-8af5-3564-b597-b765b8d3e696",
                        "source_sense_description": "genévrier : voir genévrier",
                        "target_lang_word": "juniper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "juniper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "683f3e44-5aa5-3645-b5a3-ef7d6d61dc61",
                                        "entry_id": "1cbfe363-b512-3cf2-aaf5-3e04fc554f47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any shrub or tree of the genus Juniperus of the cypress family, which is characterized by pointed, needle-like leaves and aromatic berry-like cones."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e9dd0c7-3e1f-4826-95dd-b15beeab2c3b",
                                                "sense_id": "683f3e44-5aa5-3645-b5a3-ef7d6d61dc61",
                                                "text": "On the mountains a few junipers and piñons are found, and cactuses, agave, and yuccas, low, fleshy plants with bayonets and thorns."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "785f304d-1d2f-49f3-8b28-a9e5b33ef521",
                                                "sense_id": "683f3e44-5aa5-3645-b5a3-ef7d6d61dc61",
                                                "text": "Have a tree or two the witches particularly like, such as the alder, larch, cypress and hemlock; then, to counteract any possible evil effects, there must be a holly, yew, hazel, elder, mountain ash or juniper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ce0bc42-7f3a-4775-88c0-621a8d0740ff",
                                                "sense_id": "683f3e44-5aa5-3645-b5a3-ef7d6d61dc61",
                                                "text": "Sometimes I lost track of them and had to hunt round in a circle, thrusting through sharp-scented bushes, scratching myself on various plants which were still new to me: resinaceous rock-roses, juniper [translating genévriers], ilex, yellow and white asphodel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8482f74b-2e23-4a47-9049-8663ef39312e",
                                                "sense_id": "683f3e44-5aa5-3645-b5a3-ef7d6d61dc61",
                                                "text": "One typical Grecian kiln engorged one thousand muleloads of juniper wood in a single burn. Fifty such kilns would devour six thousand metric tons of trees and brush annually."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35eb0b81-a208-305d-a828-39fe6cba376c",
                                        "entry_id": "1cbfe363-b512-3cf2-aaf5-3e04fc554f47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of a number of coniferous trees which resemble junipers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5384e3bb-2a4c-3eb7-910d-0c13d92ff48e",
                                        "entry_id": "1cbfe363-b512-3cf2-aaf5-3e04fc554f47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8882621-7ddc-4bc7-9d57-d8fe5755176a",
                                                "sense_id": "5384e3bb-2a4c-3eb7-910d-0c13d92ff48e",
                                                "text": "[…] I said you didn't like them ere strong liquors, but if he warn't particular, I was sure you would pledge him in a glass of juniper, for I had always made you, since we had been man and vife^([sic]), take a drop afore you went to market, to keep cold out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
